  "text_md": "![](<08f3aeec1eda1a569d0c9ef7bb892b5cb6a81b5b_page_1_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nMedix\n\nBiochemica\n\nIMedixMAB\"\n\n![](<08f3aeec1eda1a569d0c9ef7bb892b5cb6a81b5b_page_1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n\nANTIBODIES\n\nDate: 2019-03-15\n\n# PRODUCT SPECIFICATIONS\n\nName\n\nSpecificity\n\nDescription\n\nProduct code\n\nProduct buffer solution\n\nShelf life and storage\n\nAnalyte description\n\nAnti-h AMH 11305 SPTN-5\n\nAntibody recognizes human anti-Müllerian hormone (AMH)\n\nMonoclonal mouse antibody, cultured in   vitro under conditions free from animalderived components\n\n100760\n\n50 mM Na-citrate, pH 6.0, 0.9 % NaCI, 0.095 % NaN 3 as a preservative\n\nAnti-Müllerian hormone (AMH) is a glycoprotein produced by the Sertoli cells of the testis and by the granulosa cells of the ovary. It is used as biomarker to assess ovarian reserve levels.\n\n# PARAMETERS TESTED ON EACH LOT\n\nProduct appearance\n\nLiquid, may turn slightly opaque during storage\n\nProduct concentration\n\nImmunoreactivity\n\nIEF Profile\n\n5.0 mg/ml (+/10 %)\n\n80–120 % compared to the reference sample in an FIA test\n\n6.6 7.0\n\nPurity\n\n≥ 95 %\n\n# PARAMETERS DETERMINED DURING PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT\n\nSubclass\n\nAssociation rate constant\n\nIgG 1\n\nNot Determined (N/D)\n\nDissociation rate constant\n\nAffinity constant\n\nDetermination method\n\nDetermination antigen\n\nN/D\n\nN/D\n\n",
